Subject: [PATCH 06942/11362] [outer-loop] add object-hash identity tracking +
 containment/adjacency to color-blob salience (task 10)

Task 10 of ops/known-issues.md's 2026-07-11 SOTA-ingestion queue ("folds into
task 2, do not run as a separate experiment"). Before starting, confirmed
task 2's BASE mechanism (classical connected-component segmentation +
5-tier salience action prioritization, arXiv:2512.24156) was already shipped
and live (ColorBlobSaliencePrior, SUBMITTED_COLOR_BLOB_SALIENCE_ENABLED in
arc_competition_agent.py) -- avoided duplicating it. Task 10's two missing
sub-components, identified from an independent read of a real top-3
ARC-AGI-3 competitor's ("Duck Harness") open-sourced segmentation code
(external/duck-harness, read-only reference clone), were genuinely absent:
translation-invariant object-identity hashing and a containment/adjacency
graph over the blob list.

Added both additively to arc_color_blob_salience.py: object_hash(blob) (sha1
of color + cell-shape normalized to the blob's own bounding-box origin, so
the same shape+color hashes identically regardless of position) and
blob_topology(frame) (the frame's full unfiltered connected-component
partition -> a containment tree via complement flood-fill per blob, plus a
4-connected adjacency list). Both are pure functions over the existing
ColorBlob/connected_color_blobs primitives -- no change to ColorBlob's
fields, connected_color_blobs' signature, or any existing tier/score/
click_points behavior. Reimplemented cleanly from the reference (inspiration
tier per the project's untrusted-code-audit discipline, not copied) in this
project's own style, independently verified with fresh unit tests rather
than trusting the reference's own test suite.

Prototyped against the offline dev sim per task 2's own instruction
("prototype first, then wire into the live policy"): exp5591 segments 5 real
games' initial frames (7-68 blobs, genuine containment depth 2-3, not
degenerate), then takes a real action and checks whether any object_hash
value persists -- the load-bearing claim behind building this at all
(position-invariant identity across a REAL transition, not just a synthetic
grid). Confirmed on 5/5 games (cd82, m0r0, sk48, sp80, tu93).
adversarial_verify.py and the ARC artifact lint both clean.

Pure additive data, not yet wired into a live consuming mechanism (e.g.
preferring an object whose hash was seen to change in a prior frame) --
per the Phase Prototype + Empirical Validation discipline, deciding HOW to
use this data live is a distinct, separately-scoped design + measurement
step, not done here.

11 new tests (5 direct unit tests for object_hash/blob_topology on synthetic
grids covering translation invariance, shape/color discrimination, nested
containment, and full-pixel-partition coverage; 6 for the exp5591 prototype
script covering the blocked-precondition path, both synthetic outcome
classes, the containment-depth helper, and the checked-in real-run
artifact).

